course: dictionary
lesson: 5475
title: Laser: a narrow beam of light
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A laser is a machine that makes a very narrow, strong beam of light of one colour. The word can mean the machine or the beam itself, so look at the words around it to see which one is meant.
explain: «Lidar is a spinning laser that measures the distance to everything by timing how long its light takes to come back.» Here the laser is the machine, because it spins and it measures. The clue is the job it does.
explain: «Never shine a laser pointer at someone's eyes, at animals, cars or planes.» The warning tells you a laser is not a harmless torch. Strong light can blind people, so the sentence gives you the clue that lasers are powerful.
fact: A laser makes a very narrow, strong beam of light of one colour.
fact: «Laser» can mean the machine that makes the light, or the beam itself.
fact: Lasers are used in barcode scanners, eye surgery, measuring distances, cutting metal and light shows.
fact: «Laser pointer», «laser beam», «laser printer» and «laser tag» are all phrases that use the word laser.
fact: Never shine a laser pointer at someone's eyes, at animals, cars or planes: it can blind people.
exercise: «Lidar is a spinning laser that measures the distance to everything.» What does laser mean in this sentence? | A flat, wide sheet of paper | *A machine that makes a narrow, strong beam of light | A loud noise made by a computer | A kind of cat toy
exercise: «Cats chase a laser dot because it moves like prey, but it can never be caught.» Why should play end with a real toy? | *So the cat can catch and grab something, instead of getting frustrated | So the cat will sleep | So the cat can see the laser dot better | So the laser dot can run away faster
exercise: A laser makes a very narrow beam of light. What is the opposite of narrow? | Thin | *Wide | Dim | Hot
test: In «laser tag», what is a laser most likely used for? | Cleaning the floors | Cooking dinner | Growing plants | *A game where players tag each other with harmless beams
test: Which of these is a safe thing to do with a laser pointer? | Shine it at a friend's eyes | *Point it at a blank wall | Shine it at a cat | Shine it at a passing plane
exam: «Some are still being discovered with lasers fired from aeroplanes.» What does this tell you about lasers? | *They can be used to find hidden places from the air | They can only be used to make sounds | They are used to cook food | They are only used in toys
